practiceProblems.description:
A developer wrote a constructor but accidentally added `void`:

```java
class Laptop {
    String status;
    void Laptop() {
        status = "Configured";
    }
}
```

Because of `void`, Java treated it as a method! When `new Laptop()` runs, the method does not execute, leaving `status` as `null`.

• Remove `void` from `Laptop()` so it becomes a real constructor.
• In `Main`, instantiate `Laptop` and verify by printing: `Laptop Status: Configured`.

